  "notes": "Sheet 0 (Verónica Durán Sela's El Vasco boulevard, Oviedo, a 120,000 m2 leisure, culture, food and sports complex): a long concrete promenade deck raised above the street, wide and empty, with a pale metal-and-panel commercial building along its back whose upper storey is a long band of green glass and whose ground floor is a dark arcade; at intervals glass lift towers each beside a white perforated-panel column topped by a rounded 'arch' head; glass-floored bridges reach from one tower to the deck; behind, a white eight-storey apartment block with a regular grid of windows, and a brick block with balconies at the west. Modelled: the deck, the arcade building with its green glass band, three lift towers with their white columns and heads, two bridges, the white and brick blocks, street trees, lamp posts and a ramp. Not seen and guessed: the full extent of the complex (only a plaza and the building's one end are visible in the photographs), the cinema and sports halls (not in the pictures), every dimension, the tower positions. A public leisure complex."
